WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
- [Kelly] You're a new
book is full of stories

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.830
about cool musicians.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.340
Like when your daughter, this is amazing.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.690
Your daughter had her like,
basically her first piano lesson

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.260
from Paul McCartney.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.360
What is your life?

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.550
- It's really weird.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.690
That's what the book is
about, how weird my life is.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.590
- [Kelly] This is why I didn't
think you would remember me.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.480
Because, Paul McCartney taught
your daughter to play piano.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.120
- [Dave] I was going to put
you in the book and then they.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:20.953
- [Kelly] I didn't allow it.

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:22.410
- [Dave] It wouldn't fit, it
wouldn't fit next book that

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.243
the sequel.

00:00:23.243 --> 00:00:24.477
- [Kelly] I was like, oh
my God, that's amazing,

00:00:24.477 --> 00:00:27.010
and your daughter had no idea
how cool that moment was.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:31.630
- No, so I grew up, the
Beatles were my favorite band

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.463
and still are.

00:00:32.463 --> 00:00:33.340
And so when I was young,

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.050
I didn't take lessons to play music,

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.560
I just had Beatles records
and a Beatles song but,

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.133
years later I wound up
meeting Paul McCartney.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:45.320
And over time we played music
together, we became friends.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.660
He really is like the sweetest,

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.192
Most lovely-
Friends with the Beatles!

00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:49.025
Okay, keep going-
It's crazy.

00:00:49.025 --> 00:00:50.290
And, and I never forget that.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.280
Like, he's the nicest guy
in the world, but you know,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.360
every once in a while it
clicks, you're like, "oh my God,

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.310
I'm sitting with a Beatle right now,

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.450
I'm sitting with a Beatle".

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.283
- [Kelly] He is super nice though,

00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:58.230
so I met him once very quickly,

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.680
we were in the same studio,
like doing stuff and in passing,

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.620
he was so sweet.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.080
- So when, when my third
daughter Ophelia was born,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.077
he was in town, he was like,

00:01:06.077 --> 00:01:07.320
"Hey, we want to come see the baby".

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.520
And so they came over to the house,

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.763
and we had pizza, we're drinking wine.

00:01:10.763 --> 00:01:11.596
- With Paul McCartney.

00:01:11.596 --> 00:01:12.710
- With Paul McCartney.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:16.190
Listen! you never realize how
much Beatles stuff you have

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.023
in your house.

00:01:17.023 --> 00:01:17.856
- Until your embarrassed.

00:01:17.856 --> 00:01:19.220
- Until a Beatle comes home.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:20.620
And then you're like hiding everything,

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.700
you're like, "oh my God,
there's a coffee table books"

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:23.533
- Don't look like a tool
don't look like a tool.

00:01:23.533 --> 00:01:24.366
- Flipping out.

00:01:24.366 --> 00:01:26.120
And so as he was leaving,

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.250
there's a piano near the
front door and he sits down,

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.313
and he just starts playing Lady Madonna.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.610
In my living room!

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.610
I'm like, "Oh my God".

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:38.880
And so he's like playing.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.880
And my daughter Harper
goes into the kitchen,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.089
and she grabs a coffee cup and
she puts some change in it,

00:01:45.089 --> 00:01:47.490
and puts it on the piano
like it's a tip jar.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.323
- No!

00:01:49.529 --> 00:01:50.740
- I was like.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.940
- That's amazing.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.260
- And then she sits down next to him,

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.690
and she had never played piano before,

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:57.890
and he starts showing her like,

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.820
here's the C and these are the notes.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.810
And the two of them sat
down and started playing,

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.220
and they wrote a song together.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.690
And that was her first lesson.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.390
- Oh my gosh, that's so much cooler

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.643
than anything my kids have done.

00:02:08.643 --> 00:02:09.950
(audience laughing)
(Clapping)

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.460
- Like what!

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.697
That's incredible

